    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32-a5">

                <pb facs="0153" n="45" xml:id="pg45"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 485.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Senhor
                            Pereira.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-08-16"><hi rendition="#italic">August 16,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the note of the 5th instant,
                    in which your excellency informs me that you had on that date addressed your
                    colleague, the minister of industry, communication, and public works, upon the
                    proposition to permit cipher telegrams from the United States of America to the
                    city of Santos, and have all such telegrams translated by a Brazilian official,
                    as suggested in my note of the 3d instant, I am constrained by the great
                    importance of the question to inquire of your excellency if the matter has not
                    yet been determined.</p>
                <p>Hoping for an early and favorable reply,</p>
                <p>I improve the occasion to renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
